Third-party components
----------------------

podalign itself does not link against any GPL library. All audio processing
is performed by invoking `ffmpeg` as a subprocess.

However, podalign REQUIRES an ffmpeg build with librubberband enabled
(the `rubberband` audio filter) for clock-drift correction.

  - Rubber Band Library (librubberband) is licensed under GPLv2+.
    Source: https://github.com/breakfastquay/rubberband
  - An ffmpeg binary built with `--enable-librubberband` is a GPL build
    of ffmpeg as a whole. Source: https://ffmpeg.org/

If you distribute a container image or bundle that includes such an ffmpeg
binary (as the official podalign Docker image does), you must comply with
the GPL for those components: state that they are included (this file),
and provide access to their source code. The official Docker image uses
the unmodified Debian packages of ffmpeg and librubberband; their exact
corresponding sources are available from https://sources.debian.org/ and
via `apt-get source ffmpeg rubberband` on the image's Debian release.
